# Shared54 primary import recorder proposal

`run_import.proposed.py` is source-ready and Python AST syntax-checked. It has not been imported, executed or used to freeze inputs. The original Shared53 recorder remains unchanged. `proposal.json` records exact helper/original/engine pins and an explicitly non-authorizing assignment template.

Root first selects the registry's descriptive status correction and canonical L4 fixture CLI alias. Root then supplies actual post-selection HEAD/dev.py/registry/status/alias pins in `assignment.json` with explicit authorization for this one necessary primary import. The helper refuses before freezing without that authorization and matching pins. No project, registry, UID, ledger, Git, canonical or worker changes are made by this proposal.

The prospective command is exactly `python3 -B scripts/dev/dev.py import`. The canonical CLI owns its shared queue,300-second post-acquisition deadline and engine-child closure. The recorder adds no queue timeout, direct Godot command, suite, foreign process intervention or lock manipulation.

Before that future command, the helper inventories462 unique actual active UIDs with `.gdignore` boundaries respected, captures active native sources/import sidecars plus protected settings/design/ledger/registry, and preserves each selected original's SHA/size/mode and bytes. Selected derived cache inputs are separate. All native/UID/protected changes are nonclean; sidecar changes require Root's explicit preselected path qualification. Complete raw bytes, before/after manifests, actual command/binary pin and normal terminal closure remain preserved.

The isolated625/0 registration/import0 and primary-source PASS are reused without rerunning. This necessary import supplies no additional gameplay, portrait, full-route or acceptance credit. Old failures and uninspected current far/DASH/SPENT pixels remain disclosed. Root alone publishes Shared54 and canonical acceptance after independent review.
